---
// The personal column: a short bio and the MYSTERY quote, whose opening letters light up one by one.
---

<section class="profile paper" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <!-- The newswire is the page's one moving strip, so this heading stands still. -->
  <h2 class="column-title page" id="about-title" data-reveal="headline">The personal column</h2>
  <div class="profile-grid page">
    <figure data-reveal>
      <h3 class="personal-headline">
        A story to tell.<br /><em>A coffee to pour.</em>
      </h3>
      <p class="byline">From the personal pages of Ahmed Ali</p>
      <!-- Each button controls only its own opening letter, spelling MYSTERY down the story. -->
      <blockquote class="mystery-quote" id="mystery-quote">
        <p>
          <button
            class="story-word"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Highlight M in Midnight"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            <span class="story-initial">M</span>idnight
          </button>{" "}
          finds me with a coffee and a puzzle missing its last piece.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button
            class="story-word"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Highlight Y in You"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            <span class="story-initial">Y</span>ou
          </button>{" "}
          could call it curiosity; I call it a good evening.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button
            class="story-word"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Highlight S in Some"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            <span class="story-initial">S</span>ome
          </button>{" "}
          nights, I follow true-crime clues; others, I disappear into a
          video game.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button
            class="story-word"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Highlight T in Then"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            <span class="story-initial">T</span>hen
          </button>{" "}
          it’s a new hand of Magic: The Gathering and a different mystery
          to solve.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button
            class="story-word"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Highlight E in Every"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            <span class="story-initial">E</span>very
          </button>{" "}
          card, clue and plot twist keeps me wondering what comes next.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button
            class="story-word"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Highlight R in Reaching"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            <span class="story-initial">R</span>eaching
          </button>{" "}
          for a camera, I turn those little stories into photos and films.
        </p>
        <p>
          <button
            class="story-word"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Highlight Y in Yet"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            <span class="story-initial">Y</span>et
          </button>{" "}
          there’s always another rabbit hole and time for one more
          coffee.
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="clue-hint label">
        Hover or tap an opening letter. Read between the lines.
      </p>
    </figure>
    <div class="profile-copy" data-reveal>
      <p>
        I’m a software developer based in Hamilton, Ontario. I studied Software Development at Mohawk College. I work
        across full-stack web applications, games and visual media.
      </p>
      <p>
        I enjoy the details: tracing a bug, shaping an interaction or connecting a front end to the data behind it. I write clean,
        testable code and see projects through to deployment.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside the code, I make videos, edit photos and produce short
        films. That interest in visual storytelling carries into the
        software and games I build.
      </p>
      <dl class="profile-facts">
        <div>
          <dt>Education</dt>
          <dd>Mohawk College · Software Development</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Focus</dt>
          <dd>Java · Full-stack web · Game development</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
